(In the 1970s Winfried Honig, known as Mr Honey, started compiling and) Tj T*
(computerizing English/German dictionaries, partly to provide his) Tj T*
(colleagues and students with samples of the language of business,) Tj T*
(partly to collect convincing material for his State Department of) Tj T*
(Education to illustrate the need for special dictionaries covering) Tj T*
(the special language used in different branches of the industry.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In 1997 Mr Honey began to feed his wordlists into the LEO Online) Tj T*
(Dictionary http://dict.leo.org of the Technische Universität München,) Tj T*
(and in 2000 into the DicData Online Dictionary http://www.dicdata.de) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(While more than 500.000 daily visitors use the online versions,) Tj T*
(CD-ROM versions are available, see: http://www.leo.org/dict/cd_en.html) Tj T*
(http://www.dicdata.de http://mrhoney.purespace.de/latest.htm) Tj T*
(Mr. Honey would be pleased to answer questions sent to) Tj T*
(winfried.honig@online.de.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Permission granted to use the word-lists, on condition that links to) Tj T*
(the sites of LEO, DICDATA and MR HONEY are maintained.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Mr Honey's services are non-commercial to promote the language of) Tj T*
(business both in English and in German.-------------------) Tj T*
